{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\n\n\nstruct DSU\n{\n\tvector<ll> parent;\n\n\tDSU(ll n)\n\t{\n\t\tparent = vector<ll>(n);\n\t\tfor (ll i = 0LL; i < n; i++) {\n\t\t\tparent[i] = i;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tll find_set(ll a)\n\t{\n\t\tif (a == parent[a]) {\n\t\t\treturn a;\n\t\t}\n\t\tll base = find_set(parent[a]);\n\t\tparent[a] = base;\n\t\treturn base;\n\t}\n\n\tvoid union_set(ll a, ll b)\n\t{\n\t\ta = find_set(a);\n\t\tb = find_set(b);\n\t\tif (a != b) {\n\t\t\tif (rand() % 2) {\n\t\t\t\tswap(a, b);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tparent[b] = a;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n};\n\nll count_cycles(ll p, ll k)\n{\n\tDSU dsu(p);\n\tfor (ll i = 1LL; i < p; i++) {\n\t\tll ki = (k * i) % p;\n\t\tdsu.union_set(i, ki);\n\t}\n\n\tvector<bool> found(p, false);\n\tll count = 0LL;\n\tfor (ll i = 1LL; i < p; i++) {\n\t\tll base = dsu.find_set(i);\n\t\tif (!found[base]) {\n\t\t\tfound[base] = true;\n\t\t\tcount++;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn count;\n}\n\nll count_solutions(ll p, ll k)\n{\n\tll cycles;\n\tif (k == 0) {\n\t\tcycles = p - 1;\n\t}\n\telse if (k == 1) {\n\t\tcycles = p;\n\t}\n\telse {\n\t\tcycles = count_cycles(p, k);\n\t}\n\n\tll count = 1LL;\n\tfor (ll i = 0LL; i < cycles; i++) {\n\t\tcount *= (ll)p;\n\t\tcount %= MOD;\n\t}\n\treturn (ll)count;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n\tll p, k;\n\tcin >> p >> k;\n\tll count = count_solutions(p, k);\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\", count);\n\n\tint end;\n\tcin >> end;\n\treturn 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    static class DSU {\n        long[] parent;\n\n        DSU(int n) {\n            parent = new long[n];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                parent[i] = i;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long find_set(long a) {\n            if (a == parent[(int)a]) {\n                return a;\n            }\n            long base = find_set(parent[(int)a]);\n            parent[(int)a] = base;\n            return base;\n        }\n\n        void union_set(long a, long b) {\n            a = find_set(a);\n            b = find_set(b);\n            if (a != b) {\n                if (Math.random() < 0.5) {\n                    long temp = a;\n                    a = b;\n                    b = temp;\n                }\n                parent[(int)b] = a;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static long count_cycles(long p, long k) {\n        DSU dsu = new DSU((int)p);\n        for (long i = 1; i < p; i++) {\n            long ki = (k * i) % p;\n            dsu.union_set(i, ki);\n        }\n\n        boolean[] found = new boolean[(int)p];\n        long count = 0;\n        for (long i = 1; i < p; i++) {\n            long base = dsu.find_set(i);\n            if (!found[(int)base]) {\n                found[(int)base] = true;\n                count++;\n            }\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    static long count_solutions(long p, long k) {\n        long cycles;\n        if (k == 0) {\n            cycles = p - 1;\n        } else if (k == 1) {\n            cycles = p;\n        } else {\n            cycles = count_cycles(p, k);\n        }\n\n        long count = 1;\n        for (long i = 0; i < cycles; i++) {\n            count *= p;\n            count %= MOD;\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long p = scanner.nextLong();\n        long k = scanner.nextLong();\n        long count = count_solutions(p, k);\n        System.out.println(count);\n\n        // Read extra input to match original behavior\n        int end = scanner.nextInt();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00022301571152638644, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.002031407319009304, -2.52720492426306e-05, -0.007715070620179176, -0.036734942346811295, -0.00030322244856506586, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.00011216964776394889, -0.4287031292915344, -0.026602648198604584, -0.10500344634056091, -0.0006874820101074874, -3.6954195820726454e-05, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.4293806850910187, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -7.390948667307384e-06, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.002763026859611273, -7.748573807475623e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -6.818538531661034e-05, -6.556489552167477e-06, -4.053033626405522e-05, 0.0, -0.10085482895374298, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3245540432981215e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.6464111215318553e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.847726889536716e-05, -7.271740287251